HST Office: Writer's Home and Insert tabs as in the approved 1.0.2 ribbon mockup.

- Labels follow the reference suite at every width (owner decision of 16/11/2026). Clipboard, Editing and Text are
  groups of three rows: the large buttons fill the three rows, the small labelled buttons fill columns top to
  bottom (Cut, Copy, Format Painter; Find, Replace, Select; AutoText, Fontwork, Drop Caps, Field, Signature Line,
  Date, Object), the caption sits in row 3 and the separator spans four rows. Format Painter, Object and Select
  become small labelled buttons (Select with its 16 px image). Illustrations shows all five commands large,
  as the reference does at full width; the ladder stacks them small and labelled at the medium state.
- Font: the plain Shadow button gives way to a small "Text Effects" menu button (Shadow, Outline, Small
  Capitals), which keeps the reference suite's KeyTip F,T (owner decision of 15/11/2026).
- Paragraph: the mockup's two rows (lists | indents, hanging indent | sort, formatting marks; alignment |
  line spacing | shading, borders) in nine toolboxes, so the small state can lay them out in three rows of
  four and hide hanging indent, sort and borders (HstRibbonLadder.cxx). Text direction and paragraph
  spacing leave the Home tab: they stay in the Paragraph dialog and in the Line Spacing menu.
- Select and Shapes, menu buttons without a command, get their tooltip description from the .ui.
- Styles no longer expands, so the ladder reserves no room for previews it cannot show.
- The ribbon's root box has no top, bottom or right margin and a 4 px left one: the tab row, the 106 px body
  and the banner are placed by the tab control.
Command and widget ids are kept, except the paragraph toolboxes (bxHomeIndent, bxHomeHanging, bxHstSort,
bxHomeMarks, bxHomeAlign, bxHomeLineSpacing, bxHomeShading, bxHstBorders). The new strings get empty
entries in the Vietnamese sw/messages.po, filled by l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl.

